From ad917eacf1f24efc3960b382ef28efb8e5d993a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:53:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] hw: every whole-file save gets the empty, size and binary
 checks

Why: POST /api/config refused an empty text, a text over 256 KiB and a
text with a NUL byte, as 1.6.0's saveHardwareConfigFile does
(src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp:5325-5341 at upstream-1.6.0). The other two
whole-file doors, set_controls text= (Undo, history restore) and
set_controls restore=true, skipped those checks and handed any text to
the store.

What: the set_controls branch runs checkHardwareConfigText on the text,
after restore=true has resolved it and before the store sees it, and
replies with the same sentence as POST /api/config. The checks stay in
App, where 1.6.0 has them. They run before the store's base test, so
an empty text is refused whatever base it names.

Tested: check_core.sh both builds and host tests. --simulate run:
set_controls with text="" and with "  \n" (current and stale base) ->
"Config file cannot be empty.", a text with a NUL -> "Config file
contains invalid binary data.", 256 KiB + 1 -> "Config file is too
large."; the file stayed byte-identical. A normal text= save still
writes. POST /api/config with an empty body still gives the 1.6.0
sentence. Pi: none, no hardware path changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1w7Y8dcyiV489BiwMr
---
 src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp b/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp
index 4142407..cdded61 100644
--- a/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp
+++ b/src/ApertarCoreApp.cpp
@@ -12802,6 +12802,9 @@ std::string ApertarCoreApp::handleCommand(const ControlCommand &command)
             return errorReply(command.id, "Send the whole file (text=) or single keys (set.<section>.<key>=), not both.");
         if (!text && edits.empty())
             return errorReply(command.id, "set_controls needs text= (the whole file), restore=true, or set.<section>.<key>=value.");
+        // A whole file, restored text included, gets the same checks as POST /api/config.
+        if (std::string message; text && !checkHardwareConfigText(*text, &message))
+            return errorReply(command.id, message);
         hardware::StoreFlags flags;
         flags.backup = true;   // WebUI and core.py saves keep <file>.bak; the IMU code does not
         const std::pair<const char *, bool *> flagFields[] = {
